%% DM26-0670

%% Handing a cluster's deployment over to Polar's own git server (cluster-bootstrap.md, "Handing off to Polar's git server").
%% Built and run.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator (up.nu)
    participant Boot as Bootstrap git server (polar-deploy)
    participant Flux as Flux
    participant Git as Polar's git server
    participant Cfg as Configuration agent
    participant Att as Attestation agent

    Note over Op,Git: The bootstrap
    Op->>Boot: commit the layers, signed by the pipeline certificate, with a copy to mirror.git
    Flux->>Boot: read them, and apply them
    Flux->>Git: Polar's git server comes up, among the layers
    loop every 10 s
        Cfg->>Boot: read main, with its certificate of the deployment PKI
        Cfg->>Git: push it to deployment. The server refuses a commit the pipeline did not sign
    end

    Note over Op,Git: The handoff, once. A crash at any point resumes: where Flux reads says how far it got
    Op->>Git: wait until the copy holds the bootstrap's head
    Op->>Flux: read from Polar's git server now, while both hold the same commit
    Flux->>Git: read it
    Op->>Git: as an administrator, the commit that takes the agent's write, its settings and its key
    Git-->>Cfg: no copying from here on
    Op->>Boot: remove it. Its history stays in Polar's git server and in mirror.git, off the cluster

    Note over Op,Att: At nominal
    Op->>Git: a new deployment: a commit the pipeline signed, pushed as an administrator
    Git->>Git: verify the signature to the deployment CA, or refuse the push
    Flux->>Git: read it, and apply it
    loop every 30 s
        Cfg->>Git: read the deployment's signed record, with no write
        Cfg-)Att: publish it as it is
    end
    Att->>Att: verify it to the deployment CA, for this<br/>alone, and hold every Deployment to it

    Note over Op,Git: If the server lost its data
    Flux->>Git: bring it back, from the artifact Flux holds, empty
    Op->>Git: give it mirror.git's history, then publish on top

    Note over Op,Git: If a signed commit stops the server (up.nu --bootstrap-again), running pods keep running
    Op->>Boot: bring it back, from mirror.git, and publish the fix on top of the bad commit
    Op->>Flux: read from the bootstrap server
    Flux->>Git: apply the fix
    Op->>Op: the next run hands off again
